  "id": "procedural-justice",
  "term": "procedural justice",
  "definition": "Procedural justice is the perceived fairness of the processes an organization uses to make decisions, such as performance appraisal or pay allocation. In this context, fair and transparent procedures are linked to lower feelings of deprivation and more knowledge sharing within teams.",
