      "reasons": [
        "The packet supports procedural justice as an organizational variable related to intra-team knowledge sharing and relative deprivation, but it does not explicitly define the term as “the perceived fairness of the processes an organization uses to make decisions.”",
        "The second sentence is broader than the packet’s wording: the source reports effects on individual and group relative deprivation and intra-team knowledge sharing, but not the general claim that fair and transparent procedures are linked to lower feelings of deprivation in all contexts."
